  "id": "crutch",
  "term": "crutch",
  "definition": "In this educational psychology context, a crutch is a support that people depend on passively in place of using or developing their own learning and self-regulation processes. It contrasts with a scaffold, which is meant to strengthen planning, monitoring, and independent problem solving.",
